  "notes": "Duo-into-solo-voice country-pop with a theatrical, hiccupped vocal delivery. The entry flags one thing as \"a real structural parameter here\" and it is authored as the arrangement's centre: \"the ballads can be drumless for whole verses (voice-and-acoustic only),\" plus a bass that is \"often absent in verse 1 entirely and entering with the first chorus as the lift.\" That is the highest drop-out probability in this section together with the sparsest kick. The uptempo grammar is the stated \"8th hats, claps and tambourine over a straight backbeat.\" Harmony is \"I–V–vi–IV and IV–I–V–vi,\" with the entry's note that \"'Stay' is a near-static two-chord confessional built on I–IV alternation\" authored as its own family and a real `vamp` weight. Melody is the most distinctive claim in the batch: \"the most idiosyncratic phrasing in the section — deliberate glottal hiccups, syllable elongation and spoken interjections; wide range with sudden register jumps,\" which is why the octave-jump probability and the empty-bar bias are both high against a two-octave register. ⚠ Confidence is medium (research: medium-high); the per-track readings are [LOW-CONF] and the entry notes 160–184 figures fold to ~80–92. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are the drop-out probability, the clap offsets and the counter ratio.",
